  "query_preview": "..A trough stretches from the Great Basin into western\nArizona early this morning. This feature will move eastward across\nthe state through the day. There is enough low level moisture for\nsome lower cloud decks this morning, but moisture is too shallow\nfor precipitation except in far northern Arizona north of a Grand\nCanyon to Window Rock line. Isolated rain and snow showers are\nforecast in this area later this morning through the afternoon, \nwith snow levels 6000-6500 ft. Spotty light accumulation of less \nthan 1\" possible for the higher mountains above 7500 feet.\n\nTuesday through the weekend - fair weather is expected through the\nperiod. High pressure will be over the region Tuesday, with weak\ntroughing on Wednesday. The mid week trough continues to look too\ndry for any precipitation in our area. Stronger ridging is\nforecast over our region by Thanksgiving into the weekend, with\ndaytime temperatures reaching 5-10 degrees above normal. The next\nchance of precipitation could arrive just beyond the 7 day\nforecast early next week so stay tuned.",
